    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Concerning EU AI Act, our company context shows that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have expertise in this area and are aware of prohibited AI practices." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also prioritize human oversight and transparency in Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "AI solutions, which aligns with the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To mitigate potential legal risks, I recommend ensuring that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. subcontractors are thoroughly vetted and compliant with relevant regulatory frameworks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. should also review Nexus Engineering S.r.l. existing contracts and agreements to guarantee that our existing contracts and agreements meet the client's requirements for explicability, transparency, and human oversight." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given we current legal standing and procurement experience across EU jurisdictions, I believe we can demonstrate compliance with the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, it is crucial to conduct a thorough review of we policies and procedures to ensure that we meet all necessary regulatory standards and can provide evidence of we compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on the project, and how can our optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the company context, the standard daily rates for various roles are provided, but there is no direct information on how the standard daily rates for various roles would translate to a project of this scale." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, our do have information on the target gross margin percentage, which is 28%, and the minimum acceptable margin percentage, which is 18%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given The global budget for the project, our annual revenue from the project would be approximately 750,000 euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected, our can consider the cost sensitivity information provided." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The fixed costs are 35% of the project, and variable costs are 65%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This suggests that our have some flexibility to adjust our variable costs, such as renegotiating rates with subcontractors or optimizing resource allocation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without more specific information on the project requirements and how the project's requirements align with the standard daily rates for various roles, it is challenging to provide a precise projected margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "If our aim for the target gross margin percentage, which is 28%, our cost base for the annual revenue of 750,000 euros would need to be around 540,000 euros (750,000 * (1 - 0.28))." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve this while guaranteeing the quality of service, our would need to carefully manage both our fixed and variable costs, potentially through efficient project management, effective resource allocation, and ensuring that our delivery model aligns closely with the client's needs without incurring unnecessary expenses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk118> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of optimizing costs, considering the constraint that the annual cost of exploitation must be compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities, our would need to work closely with the client to understand the client budget constraints and ensure our pricing and cost structure aligns with their budget constraints. work might involve phasing project deliverables, prioritizing certain aspects of the project, or identifying areas where costs can be shared or reduced without compromising service quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk119> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the information available, it's clear that achieving the target gross margin percentage, which is 28% while meeting the client's budgetary constraints will require careful financial planning and management throughout the project lifecycle." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client seeks a solution that assists agents in agents daily missions by facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we leverage we AI capabilities (LLM stack, RAG, fine-tuning methods) to design an intelligent assistance tool that meets these requirements while ensuring a high level of relevance and contextual understanding?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address The client needs, we can utilize we LLM expertise, specifically we experience with models like Mistral 7B, which is we preferred sovereign model due to its strong performance on French language tasks, EU origin, and self-hostable nature under an Apache 2.0 license.  we can leverage we fine-tuning methods such as LoRA or QLoRA to adapt its to The client specific domain, improving its ability to understand contextual nuances and provide relevant answers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given that we have achieved an average accuracy gain of 12% from fine-tuning, leverage could significantly enhance its performance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, integrating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities can facilitate access to information by allowing the model to retrieve relevant documents or passages from a knowledge base and then generate answers based on a knowledge base. we experience with various retrieval strategies such as dense vector semantic search and BM25 sparse retrieval can help in achieving high precision in information retrieval, which is crucial for reducing processing times and improving answer quality. we RAG capabilities, combined with we expertise in vector stores like Qdrant, Weaviate, pgvector, and FAISS, enable we to design an efficient knowledge base that supports quick and accurate information access." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "With a typical retrieval precision at 5 of 0.87 and a low hallucination rate of 2.1%, we can ensure that the provided answers are not only relevant but also trustworthy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet the client's requirement for contextual understanding, we model can be designed to consider the context window up to 32768 tokens, allowing our model to capture detailed and nuanced information about each query or task. designed is particularly useful in administrative contexts where procedures and regulations can be complex and lengthy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, ensuring explicability and transparency is crucial. we experience with explainability methods such as source citation through RAG grounding, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME will enable we to provide insights into how the model arrives at the model suggestions or answers, thereby enhancing trust in the model." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By combining these capabilities—fine-tuned LLMs, RAG, and explainability methods—we can develop an intelligent assistance tool that effectively supports agents by providing high-quality, contextually relevant information, reducing agents workload, and improving overall efficiency." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach aligns with we known trade-offs, such as balancing explicability versus performance, and ensures compliance with regulatory requirements like GDPR through appropriate data protection measures." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

